<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n113712" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χείρων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ωνος</span>, ὁ, 
			Aeol.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χέρρων</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Alc.
			<u>Supp.</u>
			8.9
		</span></i>, 
			Dor.
		 and Thess. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χιρων</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῑ</span>] <i><span class="en">
			<u>IG</u>
			12(3).360
		</span></i> (<span class="entity">Thera</span>), <i><span class="en">
			<u>Supp.Epigr.</u>
			1.248.6
		</span></i> (Thessaly, <span class="entity">iv B.C.</span>):— <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Cheiron,</i> one of the
			Centaurs, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δικαιότατος Κενταίρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					11.832
				</span></i>
			; son of Cronus and Philyra, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				1001
			</span></i>, etc.: teacher of Achilles, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i> l. c., <i><span class="en">
				16.143
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				19.390
			</span></i>; of Asclepius and Jason, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				3.53
			</span></i>; worshipped as the father of the Art of Medicine, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.647a
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χείρωνος ὑποθῆκαι,</span>
			title of a poem ascribed to <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Quint.
				<u>Inst.</u>
				1.1.15
			</span></i>, Sch. <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				6.16
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χείρωνος ῥίζα,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάνακες τὸ Χειρώνειον</span>
			 (v. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χειρώνειος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				500
			</span></i>.</div>
